seg-f3b0a26ff5b3 = The < { "5" } m "green" bar is met for <b>Galileo MEO</b> ({ "0.13" } m dynamic) and <b>Swarm-A LEO</b> ({ "2.69" } m dynamic / { "0.10" } m reduced-dynamic). <b>LRO lunar is published as-is at { "12.05" } m dynamic / { "6.67" } m reduced-dynamic ({ "1" }+2-per-rev empirical) — above the bar</b> ({ "0.36" }, after the ME→PA offset fix; { "12.6" } / { "6.65" } m before it). A DE-grade cross-validation (above) <b>tested and corrected</b> the limiting-factor claim: the reduced-dynamic floor is <b>not</b> the analytic orientation/ephemeris (DE440 kernels leave it unchanged at { "6.67" } m), so it is not closed by better frames but by modelling the LRO non-gravitational dynamics — the honest, updated path to metre level.

